From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Settings › Displays › Cast (ADR-034)

A Cast row in Displays opens a page with the choices that apply to every
cast, bound to org.projectluma.cast (shipped by luma-cast):
- Silence Notifications (silence-notifications): the Shell holds banners as
  runtime state while casting.
- Sound (default-audio): on the screen you cast to, or on this computer.
- Allow Screens That Connect Directly (allow-wifi-direct).

Remembered Screens lists GetRememberedDevices from org.projectluma.Cast1 with
the last choice, when it was used and whether it is nearby; each can be pinned
(SetPinned) or forgotten (ForgetDevice, after a confirmation). The list
follows DevicesChanged. Without luma-cast the page says casting isn't
available and offers nothing that does nothing.

`gnome-control-center display cast` (Quick Settings › Cast › Cast Settings)
opens Displays directly on the Cast page.

On top of 0001-0014; 0015 is reserved for the audio-policy series.
---
diff --git a/panels/display/cc-cast-page.c b/panels/display/cc-cast-page.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0c5f366
--- /dev/null
+++ b/panels/display/cc-cast-page.c
@@ -0,0 +1,550 @@
